course: dictionary
lesson: 9509
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which one the writer means. «A steward looks after passengers on a plane.» The clues are plane and passengers, so a steward is a person whose job is to look after people on a plane, ship or train.
explain: «Stay where you are and ask a steward in a bright vest.» At a big event, the bright vest and the crowd are your clues. A steward is a helper who keeps people safe and shows them where to go. The same word can mean something different in another sentence.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «a helper in a bright vest shows me where to go» make sense? Yes, so you have it right. A steward can also mean someone who looks after something precious for others, as in «We are stewards of the Earth, so we should care for it.»
fact: A steward is a person whose job is to look after people or things for others.
fact: «Steward» can mean a person who looks after passengers on a plane, ship or train.
fact: At a big match or concert, a steward helps people find their way and stay safe.
fact: «Flight attendant» is the usual modern word for a steward on a plane.
fact: We can be stewards of the Earth when we look after it for everyone.
exercise: «He stays calm, goes to a steward in a bright jacket and shows his wristband.» Where is the steward most likely working? | In a bakery | On a farm | On a train | *At a big event
exercise: What is the main job of a steward on a plane? | Sells food at the airport shop | Flies the plane | Cleans the runway | *Looks after the passengers
exercise: Ayo says, «We are stewards of the Earth.» What does steward mean here? | A loud shout | *Someone who looks after something precious for others | A type of fast boat | A person who drives a bus
test: «At a big match, children stay with their adult, agree a meeting point, and tell a steward if the crowd feels too tight.» Why would you tell a steward? | *Because the crowd feels too tight and they can help keep you safe | To ask for a snack | To say goodbye to your adult | To buy a ticket for the train
test: Mia is lost at a concert. «If you get lost at an event, go to the meeting point or ask a steward, a police officer or a staff member in uniform.» Who could Mia ask? | The ice cream seller only | Only the band on stage | Nobody, she must find her own way home | *A steward in uniform or a bright vest
exam: Which meaning of steward fits «We are stewards of the Earth, so we should care for it»? | A type of boat | A helper at a big match | *Someone who cares for the Earth for others | A plane helper
